-/-!
-# From generation of `π₂` to the vanishing of the arrows of the descended chain
-
-The last paragraph of the proof of Proposition 3.11 reads: *"For subsequent arrows, the square
-formed by `Lᵢ → Lᵢ₊₁` and `Eᵢ → Eᵢ₊₁` commutes.  The upper arrow is zero on `π₂` and its
-images generate the lower source by (3.5).  Hence every lower arrow is zero on the whole of
-`π₂`."*  This file proves exactly that implication in the combinatorial model, so that the
-only thing the paper's geometry still has to supply for those arrows is the generation
-statement (3.5) itself.
-
-* `FiniteChains.Comb.shiftHom` — **change of base vertex**: a path `q` from `y₀` to `w₀`
-  induces a cellular map `Ũ(X, w₀) → Ũ(X, y₀)` of universal covers over `X`, sending the base
-  vertex to the class of `q`.  (For a loop this is the deck transformation of
-  `RequestProject/CombUniversalCover.lean`.)
-* `FiniteChains.Comb.Pi2FromSub` — the spherical classes of `E` **coming from a subcomplex**
-  `ι : L → E`: the images of `π₂(L)` under all lifts of `ι` to the universal covers.  As the
-  lifts range over all of them, these are exactly the images of the copies of `L̃` inside
-  `Ẽ`, i.e. the translates by the deck group of the image of `π₂(L)`.
-* `FiniteChains.Comb.zeroPi2_chain_of_generated` — **the implication**: in a commuting square
-  `j ∘ ι = ι' ∘ k` with `k` zero on `π₂`, every class of `π₂(E)` in the span of
-  `Pi2FromSub ι` is killed by `j`.
-* `FiniteChains.Comb.zeroPi2_of_pi2Generated` — consequently, if `π₂(E)` is generated by the
-  classes coming from `L`, then `j` is zero on `π₂`.
--/
